# Documentation Consolidation & Sync Strategy

This plan outlines how to move and organize all your research/brain files from the system-managed Gemini directory into your project, while maintaining their chronological and chat-based context.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Multi-Category Sorting**: We will now sort files into four specific buckets:
> 1. **Tasks & Implementations** (Task lists, plans, snapshots)
> 2. **Planning & Strategies** (Architectures, roadmaps, designs)
> 3. **Learning & Walkthrough** (Guides, retrospectives, walkthroughs)
> 4. **Vision & Features** (Philosophies, master docs, visionary lists)
> 
> **Context Preservation**: A single chat session might be split across these folders if it contains multiple file types, but the session-specific folder (e.g., `2026-02-04_Auth-Setup`) will remain consistent across all categories.

## Proposed Changes

We will create a consolidation script that does the following:
1. Loops through each "Session" folder in your Brain directory.
2. Identifies the primary task or topic of that session (by reading [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d7e3ed05-2fb9-4b12-97a8-302ab75b8083/task.md)).
3. Copies all files (including [.resolved](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/ed5e0757-6cdd-4eaa-928b-7096a381c2a9/task.md.resolved) and [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d7e3ed05-2fb9-4b12-97a8-302ab75b8083/task.md)) into a structured folder in `apps/gurudevi-mobile/Docs v 3.0/brain_archive/`.

